"Further refinements: (1) rooms' outer location comes from a NEW FIELD ON THE MAP (name + kind), not per-room blobs - ALL rooms gain a location; interior maps use kind Interior (same id, different location per comparison rule, no recursion). (2) EQUIPPED items' locations become (carrier, Exterior) - the visible surface of the body - while pocketed items are (carrier, Interior); inventory checks match id alone so both count as carried. The equipment convergence (apply_resolved_equipment, the one canonical writer) also sets carried gear kinds: counted-first-N instances of worn/wielded assets go Exterior, the rest Interior."